885:      * Requirements of the different inputs of an operator. Each input can have a different
886:      * requirement. For all {@link #SORTED} inputs, records are sorted/grouped by key and all
887:      * records of a given key are passed to the operator consecutively before moving on to the next
888:      * group.
889:      */
890:     public enum InputRequirement {
891:         /**
892:          * Records from all sorted inputs are grouped (sorted) by key and are then fed to the
893:          * operator one group at a time. This "zig-zags" between different inputs if records for the
894:          * same key arrive on multiple inputs to ensure that the operator sees all records with a
895:          * key as one consecutive group.
