81:  * function from MathUtils because of its avalanche property, so that changing only some high bits
82:  * of the original value won't leave the lower bits of the hash unaffected. This is because when
83:  * choosing the bucket for a record, we mask only the lower bits (see numBucketsMask). Lots of
84:  * collisions would occur when, for example, the original value that is hashed is some bitset, where
