375:     /**
376:      * Verifies that concurrent release via the SingleInputGate and re-triggering of a partition
377:      * request works smoothly.
378:      *
379:      * <ul>
380:      *   <li>SingleInputGate acquires its request lock and tries to release all registered channels.
381:      *       When releasing a channel, it needs to acquire the channel's shared request-release
382:      *       lock.
383:      *   <li>If a LocalInputChannel concurrently retriggers a partition request via a Timer Thread
384:      *       it acquires the channel's request-release lock and calls the retrigger callback on the
385:      *       SingleInputGate, which again tries to acquire the gate's request lock.
386:      * </ul>
387:      *
388:      * <p>For certain timings this obviously leads to a deadlock. This test reliably reproduced such
389:      * a timing (reported in FLINK-5228). This test is pretty much testing the buggy implementation
390:      * and has not much more general value. If it becomes obsolete at some point (future greatness
391:      * ;)), feel free to remove it.
392:      *
393:      * <p>The fix in the end was to not acquire the channels lock when releasing it and/or not doing
394:      * any input gate callbacks while holding the channel's lock. I decided to do both.
395:      */
396:     @Test
397:     void testConcurrentReleaseAndRetriggerPartitionRequest() throws Exception {
398:         final SingleInputGate gate = createSingleInputGate(1);
399: 
400:         ResultPartitionManager partitionManager = mock(ResultPartitionManager.class);
401:         when(partitionManager.createSubpartitionView(
402:                         any(ResultPartitionID.class),
403:                         any(ResultSubpartitionIndexSet.class),
404:                         any(BufferAvailabilityListener.class)))
405:                 .thenAnswer(
406:                         (Answer<ResultSubpartitionView>)
407:                                 invocationOnMock -> {
408:                                     // Sleep here a little to give the releaser Thread
409:                                     // time to acquire the input gate lock. We throw
410:                                     // the Exception to retrigger the request.
411:                                     Thread.sleep(100);
412:                                     throw new PartitionNotFoundException(new ResultPartitionID());
413:                                 });
414: 
415:         final LocalInputChannel channel = createLocalInputChannel(gate, partitionManager, 1, 1);
416: 
417:         Thread releaser =
418:                 new Thread(
419:                         () -> {
420:                             try {
421:                                 gate.close();
422:                             } catch (IOException ignored) {
423:                             }
424:                         });
425: 
426:         Thread requester =
427:                 new Thread(
428:                         () -> {
429:                             try {
430:                                 channel.requestSubpartitions();
431:                             } catch (IOException ignored) {
432:                             }
433:                         });
434: 
435:         requester.start();
436:         releaser.start();
437: 
438:         releaser.join();
439:         requester.join();
440:     }
