60: /**
61:  * Integration test for performing the unaligned checkpoint.
62:  *
63:  * <p>This tests checks for completeness and orderness of results after recovery. In particular, the
64:  * following topology is used:
65:  *
66:  * <ol>
67:  *   <li>A source that generates unique, monotonically increasing, equidistant longs. Given
68:  *       parallelism=4, the first subtask generates [0, 4, ...], the second subtask [1, 5, ...].
69:  *   <li>A shuffle that shifts all outputs of partition i to the input of partition i+1 mod n, such
70:  *       that the order of records are retained.
71:  *   <li>A failing map that fails during map, snapshotState, initializeState, and close on certain
72:  *       checkpoints / run attempts (more see below).
73:  *   <li>A shuffle that fairly distributes the records deterministically, such that duplicates can
74:  *       be detected.
75:  *   <li>A verifying sink that counts all anomalies and exposes counters for verification in the
76:  *       calling test case.
77:  * </ol>
78:  *
79:  * <p>The tests are executed in a certain degree of parallelism until a given number of checkpoints
80:  * have been successfully taken. Tests time out to guard against infinite failure loops or if no
81:  * successful checkpoint has been taken for other reasons.
82:  *
83:  * <p>Failures are triggered on certain checkpoints to spread them evenly and run attempts to avoid
84:  * infinite failure loops. For the tests, the failures are induced in the 1. subtask after m&lt;n
85:  * successful checkpoints with n the number of successful checkpoints needed to pass the test:
86:  *
87:  * <ol>
88:  *   <li>After {@code m=1/4*n}, map fails.
89:  *   <li>After {@code m=1/2*n}, snapshotState fails.
90:  *   <li>After {@code m=3/4*n}, map fails and the corresponding recovery fails once.
91:  *   <li>At the end, close fails once.
92:  * </ol>
93:  *
94:  * <p>The following verifications are performed.
95:  *
96:  * <ul>
97:  *   <li>The number of outputs should be the number of inputs (no lost records).
98:  *   <li>No record of source subtask {@code i} can overtake a record of the same subtask
99:  *       (orderness).
100:  *   <li>No record should arrive at the sink twice (e.g., being emitted or recovered multiple
101:  *       times), which tests exactly once.
102:  *   <li>The number of successful checkpoints is indeed {@code >=n}.
103:  * </ul>
104:  */
